u('Complete User Guide',p('Autonomous Space Telemedicine &amp; Research Assistant','lead')+p('Learn what the current application does, how to operate it, and how to explain it honestly. No programming knowledge is assumed.')+shot('dashboard','Figure U1. Mission overview with fictional crew and source-bound synthetic observations.')+h('What is ASTRA?')+p('ASTRA is an offline-first research prototype for exploring crew health during a space mission. It combines monitoring, fictional mission scenarios, a selectable 3D body, recorded signal replay, trend research and local scientific evidence tools. A long communication delay makes clear onboard information and human oversight valuable.')+box('<strong>What you are demonstrating:</strong> working software with simulated crew data. The six astronauts are fictional. A real API request does not mean a real sensor measured an astronaut. ASTRA does not diagnose disease, prescribe treatment or claim flight certification.')+h('Who uses which part?')+p('Crew and mission staff view observations and review alerts. Researchers inspect model evidence and source quotations. The current login is a local demonstration identity system, not a production identity service.')+table(['Learn / do','Pages'],[['Start, login and navigation','2–3'],['Dashboard, alerts and scenarios','4–5'],['Anatomy, waveforms and personal records','6–8'],['Research boundaries and five-minute demo','9–10'],['Keys, troubleshooting and quick reference','11–12']],[77,23])+refs('package.json','apps/mission-control-web/app.mjs','services/api/server.mjs','docs/ASTRA_FINAL_DEMO_READINESS.md'),'cover')
u('Start safely: Windows or WSL',p('A <strong>terminal</strong> is a window where you type commands. Node.js runs ASTRA. npm runs named commands from <code>package.json</code>. One Node process serves both the backend and the browser interface; there is no second frontend server.')+h('1 · Check the existing installation')+code('node --version\nnpm --version')+p('Use Node <strong>24.21.0 or newer on the Node 24 line, below 25</strong>. Keep the repository’s existing packages, Three.js vendor files and local assets. No new install is needed for the previously prepared demo.')+h('2 · WSL / Ubuntu: open the project terminal and run')+code('cd /mnt/c/users/basim/onedrive/desktop/astra-space-medical-ai\ndemo_dir=$(mktemp -d /tmp/astra-presentation-XXXXXXXX)\nexport ASTRA_DB="$demo_dir/astra.sqlite"\nexport HOST=127.0.0.1 PORT=3000 ASTRA_SPEED=1\nnpm start')+h('Or Windows PowerShell')+code("Set-Location 'C:\\Users\\basim\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\ASTRA-Space-Medical-AI'\n$demoName='astra-presentation-'+[guid]::NewGuid().ToString('N')\n$demoRoot=Join-Path ([IO.Path]::GetTempPath()) $demoName\nNew-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $demoRoot | Out-Null\n$env:ASTRA_DB=Join-Path $demoRoot 'astra.sqlite'\n$env:HOST='127.0.0.1'; $env:PORT='3000'; $env:ASTRA_SPEED='1'\nnpm start")+p('The actual npm start script is <code>node services/api/server.mjs</code>; typing that directly is equivalent. If Windows Node is not on PATH, the prepared alternative is <code>.\\artifacts\\n03-windows-tools\\node.exe services/api/server.mjs</code>.')+h('3 · Open, stop and restart')+ol('Open <strong>http://127.0.0.1:3000</strong> in the browser. Keep the terminal open.','Press <strong>Ctrl+C</strong> in that terminal to stop. To recover, run npm start again with the <strong>same ASTRA_DB path</strong>. Do not create another temp directory unless you want a fresh demo.','If port 3000 is occupied, set PORT to 3001 in your current shell, then use http://127.0.0.1:3001. Do not stop an unrelated process.')+box('<strong>Settings:</strong> ASTRA_DB chooses the SQLite data file; HOST binds to your own laptop; PORT chooses the local address; ASTRA_SPEED=1 keeps the mission clock at 1×. Without these settings, the CLI defaults to data/runtime/astra.sqlite and speed 30. Use the isolated path above to protect existing runtime data.')+refs('package.json → scripts.start / engines','services/api/server.mjs → CLI environment readers'),'compact')
u('Login, roles and navigation',h('Login without revealing a secret')+ol('Open the local URL. Choose the <strong>Demo administrator</strong> role in the demo login form.','Submit the login form. This creates a local browser session. There is no password to publish in this guide.','Use the navigation menu. On narrow screens open the menu first. Use the visible Logout control to end the session.')+p('A <strong>role</strong> determines permitted actions. Authentication answers “who is this session?” Authorization answers “may this session do that?” A valid role does not grant every feature or another person’s private cognition data.')+table(['Role','Main scope / limits'],[['Demo administrator','Presentation controls, scenario and communications configuration, review and acknowledgement; not unrestricted private cognition.'],['Astronaut','Own fictional CREW-03 data, permitted check-ins and acknowledgement. Cross-crew reads are denied.'],['Mission control / Flight surgeon','Mission review and acknowledgement; additional audit/model permissions differ. Private access still needs the relevant policy.'],['Researcher','Research/model evidence and permitted reads; not alert acknowledgement or raw waveform access.'],['Viewer / System administrator','Viewer is read-only. System administrator has system/audit scope, not automatic health-read permission.']],[29,71])+h('Where to go')+table(['Workspace','What you can do'],[['Mission overview','Six crew cards, monitoring and source/communications state.'],['Crew health','Select a crew member; see vitals, evidence, history, anatomy and available trends.'],['Sleep & resilience','Sleep, exercise and consent-controlled personal context.'],['Signal archive','Permitted synthetic waveform imports and recording replay.'],['Health agent / Communications','Existing template cases; acknowledgement-linked reports and delayed Earth receipt.'],['Research library / Scenario lab','Older local knowledge search; qualified fictional mission scenarios.'],['Evidence & provenance','Source metadata, audit visibility and scoped model evidence.']],[33,67])+box('<strong>Session expiry:</strong> sessions last up to two hours. A 401 response means login is required; 403 means this role or crew scope is forbidden. Log in again when required. Do not bypass a denied request by changing IDs in the address or developer tools.')+refs('services/api/auth.mjs → createSession/getIdentity','packages/contracts.mjs → PERMISSIONS','apps/mission-control-web/app.mjs → NAV, api()'))
u('Dashboard, vitals and alerts',shot('alert','Figure U2. An acknowledged synthetic event, distinct from eventual Earth delivery.','small')+h('Read the observations, not just the color')+ol('Open Mission overview. Choose one of the six fictional crew members, then open Crew health.','Check metric, unit, observation time and quality. Open Mission replay and move its timeline slider for stored history; use the live view to return to current eligible data.','Open the recorded alert evidence for that crew. An alert is a persisted monitoring event; it may remain recorded after current measurements change.')+table(['Measurement','Meaning / unit'],[['Heart rate / heart-rate variability','Beats per minute (/min) / variability in milliseconds (ms).'],['SpO₂ / respiration / temperature','Oxygen-saturation percentage / breaths per minute / degrees Celsius.'],['Sleep / fatigue / reaction / exercise','Hours / authored 0–10 score / milliseconds / minutes.'],['Radiation','Contextual dose-rate reading in mSv/h; not an organ-damage estimate.']],[41,59])+cols(h('Monitoring states')+p('<strong>Green:</strong> no currently qualifying rule event; not a medical all-clear.<br><strong>Amber / Red:</strong> a deterministic review/escalation rule met its persistence requirement.<br><strong>Gray / UNKNOWN:</strong> missing, stale, suspect or insufficient data. Never interpret this as healthy.'),h('Acknowledge correctly')+p('With an acknowledgement-capable role, open the alert and select its acknowledgement action. Wait for confirmation. If case preparation is still pending, wait and retry the visible action. Do not claim success after a conflict or error.'))+h('Why Earth may still show older data')+p('Acknowledgement records a human decision locally. A report then follows the durable communications queue. Default one-way delay is 12 mission minutes, plus transmission and small jitter; blackout or retry can delay it further. Acknowledgement, transmission and receipt are separate events. Use Communications to inspect the queue and Spacecraft/Earth received views. Its privileged synthetic controls configure delay, bandwidth, loss and blackout; changing a setting does not mean Earth already received a report.')+refs('services/anomaly/detector.mjs → evaluateCrew/TIER_A','services/api/engine.mjs → acknowledge','services/comms/scheduler.mjs'))
u('Run a fictional health scenario',shot('scenario','Figure U3. Scenario Lab operates the actual synthetic mission service.','small')+p('A <strong>simulation</strong> generates measurements in software. A seed is a starting number that makes a run repeatable. These are useful for testing alerts, missing-data handling and recovery; they do not establish real medical performance.')+h('Reliable presentation sequence')+ol('Open Scenario lab as Demo administrator. Select <strong>CREW-03 / Amara Okafor</strong>.','Choose <strong>Cardiorespiratory drift</strong>. Use duration <strong>600 seconds</strong>, cadence <strong>30 seconds</strong> and seed <strong>42017</strong> in the available fields. Start the run.','Use the manual advance/step control for <strong>300 seconds</strong>. This is mission time, not five minutes of waiting.','Return to Crew health for CREW-03. Inspect real generated measurements and the recorded N02 event. Acknowledge through N02’s approved action.','Pause/resume using Scenario lab. Stop ends progression but retains history and alerts. Reset starts a new run; it does not erase earlier evidence.')+table(['Preset group','What it exercises'],[['Nominal / controlled HR rise','Stable conditions or a single changing metric.'],['Cardiorespiratory drift / sleep-debt cardio drift','Coordinated authored changes with persistence.'],['Sleep fatigue / post exercise','Sleep context or activity-associated changes.'],['Radiation spike','Environmental context; not automatic clinical localization.'],['Sensor dropout / contradictory sensors','Missing and suspect data; expect honest UNKNOWN.'],['Communication blackout','Delayed delivery while onboard monitoring remains separate.']],[46,54])+box('<strong>Clock warning:</strong> a paused source can become stale, so UNKNOWN may be correct. The mission/source clock differs from your laptop’s wall clock. A scenario’s authored event is not an observed emergency, and a demo score is not a clinical probability.')+h('If a command fails')+p('Wait for the pending operation to finish; check the selected run and current revision. The UI refreshes run state before a new command. An uncertain retry must preserve its request identity. Avoid double-clicking Start or repeatedly changing runs during a pending command.')+refs('services/telemetry-simulator/n09-model.mjs','services/telemetry-simulator/n09-engine.mjs','apps/mission-control-web/n09.mjs','docs/demo/PRESENTATION_CHECKLIST.md'))
u('Use the interactive 3D anatomy',shot('anatomy','Figure U4. A selected reference region with source-bound fictional crew data.')+ol('Open Crew health and verify the selected crew identity. Wait for the 3D model to finish loading.','Drag to rotate; use the wheel or touch pinch to zoom. Keyboard and visible camera controls provide alternatives. Reset restores framing.','Use layers to show/hide available surfaces. Switch detailed/coarse quality (LOD: level of detail) when needed.','Click an actual supported mesh, or use the named region buttons. Read the linked panel’s crew, units, source time, quality and monitoring evidence.','Open available history or Signal archive from the panel. Clear selection or choose another region. Changing crew must clear/replace old values.')+table(['Region','Permitted linked information'],[['Cardiovascular / heart reference','Heart rate and HRV; compatible ECG/PPG recording if present.'],['Left / right lung reference','Respiration and SpO₂; compatible RESP recording if present.'],['Body / skeleton','Body temperature / no mapped skeleton measurement: UNKNOWN.'],['Head / thorax context','Conceptual controls without extra organ geometry: completed non-private sleep context / HR and respiration.']],[34,66])+box('<strong>A navigation aid, not a diagnosis.</strong> The generic licensed model is not a scan of the selected person. Heart surfaces are incomplete. Highlighting a heart region does not prove heart disease. HR/RR-driven illustrative timing freezes when eligible source data are unavailable; it is not a validated organ-motion model.',True)+p('If graphics fail, use the textual region controls and details. Follow the reload/recovery control after context loss. Reduced-motion settings are respected. Do not keep opening duplicate tabs to solve a slow load: retained tests observed about <strong>8–9 seconds</strong> for initial crew switching with 3D remounting.')+refs('apps/mission-control-web/anatomy.mjs','apps/mission-control-web/anatomy-runtime.mjs','packages/anatomy-link.mjs','services/api/anatomy.mjs'))
u('View signals and replay recordings',shot('waveform','Figure U5. Signal archive preserves recording, channel, units and archive time.')+p('A <strong>waveform</strong> is a series of sampled values drawn over time. Its sampling rate tells you how many values were recorded each second. ASTRA’s supported demo recordings are explicitly synthetic, not a live astronaut ECG.')+h('Import and inspect an authorized synthetic recording')+ol('Open Signal archive; confirm the crew selection. Use the built-in synthetic example workflow or select an already authorized ASTRAWV1 binary / ASTRACSVv1 file.','Confirm synthetic provenance, then click Generate &amp; import once for the example or import the selected file with a permitted role. Do not upload real patient files.','Choose the recording and channel: ECG, PPG or RESP only where that source provides them. Inspect units, sampling frequency, source identity and timestamps.','Drag the archive cursor, use start/seek controls and Play/Pause. The chart follows recording time, not “live sensor” time.','Inspect missing intervals and quality flags. A gap is unavailable data, not a zero reading or an interpolated medical finding.')+h('What to expect and what may be unavailable')+p('The compact parser accepts bounded recordings: up to 256,000 bytes, 1–60 seconds, 1–3 channels and 50–500 Hz. A compatible source is required; selecting a cardiovascular region cannot manufacture an ECG. No validated blood-pressure estimate is inferred from PPG.')+box('<strong>History cutoff:</strong> a recording is visible only when it was known by the selected archive cutoff. After import the UI can advance an unchanged cutoff and announce that update. An intentionally chosen historical cutoff remains yours; choose a compatible cutoff to view a newly imported source.')+h('Common errors')+p('No recording: import an eligible synthetic example or show unavailable. Wrong channel: select one supplied by the recording. Blank signal: check cursor, cutoff and gaps. Denied import: use an authorized role, not a service token or a file-path workaround. Large or malformed files are rejected cleanly.')+refs('packages/waveforms.mjs','services/waveforms/service.mjs','apps/mission-control-web/waveforms.mjs'))
u('Sleep, exercise and private check-ins',p('Open <strong>Sleep &amp; resilience</strong> for descriptive records. Open the voluntary cognitive check-in from its existing utility control. These functions track context and authored demonstration inputs; they do not diagnose sleep disorders, depression or cognitive impairment.')+cols(h('Sleep records and schedules')+ol('Select the intended fictional crew. Read completed sleep intervals, any available stages and coverage.','Use the relevant form to record an allowed sleep interval or planned schedule. Check units and dates before saving.','Review actual duration, schedule comparison and descriptive shortfall. Missing coverage must remain visible.'),h('Exercise and movement')+ol('Open the exercise context. Inspect the plan and eligible completed sessions.','Enter a permitted synthetic session or plan using the labeled fields.','Review duration, workload and adherence history. These are descriptions of records, not a fitness prescription.'))+h('Voluntary cognition and mood')+ol('Read the consent explanation before starting. Enable only the participation/sharing choices you intend.','Complete the timed reaction task’s five trials when its target signals readiness. Early clicks are not valid reaction measurements.','Save only through the provided action. Mood/fatigue inputs are optional. Personal reference calculations need sufficient eligible same-person history.','Inspect your permitted history. A different role or actor must not gain private data simply by selecting another crew member.')+flow('Figure U6. Consent and source-bound records remain separate from operational diagnosis.',['Choose eligible crew + record type','Consent / actor / device and source checks','Append a versioned record → descriptive view'])+box('<strong>Privacy rule:</strong> administrator does not mean unrestricted access to private cognitive results. Current consent and actor/device policy still apply. N06’s conceptual head context uses completed non-private sleep context, not private reaction or mood records.')+p('If the form reports missing data, consent required or access denied, correct the permitted input or stop that workflow. Do not replace unavailable values with a fabricated “normal” score. Historical views also respect when a record became known.')+refs('services/n10/contracts.mjs','services/n10/ledger.mjs','services/n10/projection.mjs','apps/mission-control-web/n10.mjs'))
u('Research, forecasts and AI: know the limits',table(['Feature / location','How to use it honestly'],[['Crew health: conditional trends','Inspect an available trend and its coverage/horizon. Persistence repeats a last value; OLS fits a line; Theil–Sen uses a median slope. Missing/stale inputs can produce UNKNOWN. The legacy trend and full N12 research protocol differ.'],['Evidence & provenance: N11/N12','Read permitted existing model evidence and saved results. Isolation Forest was rejected. N12 has zero operational promotions. Do not click fresh Compute, train, calibrate or evaluate for this presentation.'],['Research library: in the app','Search the older local knowledge summaries. This screen is not the independently governed N13 exact-publication corpus interface. Do not equate summary citations with proven medical answers.'],['N13/N14: research/backend only','Use the offline CLI below for source verification and exact-window lexical lookup. No new dedicated NASA-corpus screen is available in the main application.'],['N15: research/backend only','Local Qwen execution was historically demonstrated. Current native execution and positive factual-support rules are inactive. Qwen is not actively answering in the app.'],['Health agent: main app','Shows deterministic N02 case summaries and suggested review steps, marked generated_by_llm:false. It is not the operational N16 four-tool coordinator.'],['N16: separate recorded demo','Open the retained standalone HTML to explain four fixed synthetic SQL tools. This replays a record; do not launch sealed-source workers.']],[33,67])+h('Permitted local evidence lookup · WSL terminal')+code('node scripts/n14-offline.mjs verify\nnode scripts/n14-offline.mjs query --policy=rich_lexical \\\n  --top_k=3 --query="light circadian sleep"')+p('Example of exact source text: “Further research is needed in this area” (NASA HRP sleep report, 2016, physical PDF page 4). This is a research caveat, not a personal diagnosis. Read the returned source identifier, exact quotation and citation. <strong>A valid quotation proves attribution, not that an answer is relevant or medically supported.</strong> Unsupported numerical or medical questions must abstain in the governed answering path; search hits alone are not an answer.')+box('<strong>AI vocabulary:</strong> retrieval finds text; an embedding represents text numerically; an LLM generates text. Current lexical lookup is deterministic. Semantic/hybrid research stays experimental; unreviewed factual rules are not activated by finding a NASA citation.')+p('Recorded agent: <code>artifacts/n16-final-20261030/native/demo.html</code>. N12 backup evidence and the silent presentation video are linked from the final demo guide; use existing records rather than starting a new model campaign.')+refs('services/prediction/forecast.mjs','services/n12/forecast.mjs','services/research-retrieval/research-service.mjs','services/research-answer/governed-service.mjs','services/agent/agent.mjs'),'compact')
u('Your five-minute demonstration',p('Prepare the isolated database and browser before judges arrive. Import the authorized synthetic waveform example and check that the chosen crew has a source. Do not spend presentation time downloading packages, fitting models or seeking new scientific approvals.')+table(['Time','Action and expected result'],[['0:00–0:35','Launch with the page 2 commands; choose Demo administrator. Show Mission overview. Say: “Six fictional crew members; locally generated observations.”'],['0:35–1:20','Select CREW-03. Show metric units, source times and quality. Open Scenario lab; start Cardiorespiratory drift with 600 s duration, 30 s cadence and seed 42017. Advance 300 s.'],['1:20–2:05','Return to CREW-03, open the genuine persisted N02 alert and evidence. Acknowledge with the permitted role. Explain that human acknowledgement queues a report; Earth has not instantly received it.'],['2:05–3:00','Open the loaded anatomy. Select Cardiovascular; rotate/reset and inspect the actual crew-linked heart rate. Explain source quality and the conceptual, non-diagnostic mapping.'],['3:00–3:40','Open matching Signal archive/history where available. Show source/channel, timestamp, gaps and Play/Pause. It is an imported synthetic recording, not a live ECG.'],['3:40–4:20','Switch crew and show that values change or become UNKNOWN. If a conditional trend is eligible, show its research label. Otherwise use the saved N12 evidence backup; do not run Compute.'],['4:20–5:00','Show the prepared N14 lexical quotation lookup, or its retained actual output. State citation ≠ factual entailment. End with the offline architecture, human review and current limitations.']],[19,81])+h('Presentation fallback ladder')+ol('If a screen is still loading, allow the observed 8–9 seconds for a crew/3D remount. Show the source-bound textual panel while it loads.','If a session expires, log in again. If the backend fails, stop and restart using the same ASTRA_DB; refresh the browser after the server is ready.','If a waveform is absent or a trend abstains, explain the truthful unavailable state. Use an existing saved result or the recorded backup; never replace it with a made-up number.')+box('<strong>Safe opening line:</strong> “ASTRA is an offline-first research prototype. Today I will demonstrate synthetic crew monitoring, human acknowledgement, source-bound anatomy and waveform replay—not a clinically validated autonomous doctor.”')+p('Retained backup: <code>docs/ASTRA_FINAL_DEMO_READINESS.md</code> links the actual successful silent recording and standalone research/agent records. The video is historical evidence, not a new recording of this documentation build.')+refs('docs/demo/PRESENTATION_CHECKLIST.md','artifacts/presentation-readiness-20261109/final-validation.json'))
u('Keys, setup and troubleshooting',table(['Service / setting','Required for this demo?'],[['OpenAI / cloud Qwen / Supabase','No. No supported demo path calls these services or needs their keys.'],['Hugging Face / NASA API','No runtime token/key. Existing local assets and downloaded-source records are separate from a new acquisition.'],['Local Qwen weights','No remote AI key, but native execution still requires current resource/sandbox approval; presently inactive.'],['SQLite credentials','None. Local file permissions and safe ASTRA_DB selection matter.'],['ASTRA_INGEST_TOKEN','Optional service credential for external scalar telemetry ingestion only. Not needed for the simulator or authorized waveform UI import. Unset means that service path is disabled.']],[37,63])+p('Configure actual settings in the terminal environment before starting. The server does not establish an automatic .env loader. Never paste a secret into source code or these PDFs.')+table(['Symptom','What to do'],[['npm start / dependency failure','Check the project directory and Node 24.21+ (&lt;25). Retain the prepared packages/vendor assets. Do not run a blind upgrade or download campaign.'],['Port 3000 in use','Choose PORT=3001 and open its matching URL. Keep HOST=127.0.0.1.'],['Backend unreachable / blank page','Read the launch terminal error; check URL/port. Restart the same DB path. If the old service worker shell persists, reload once online.'],['Database unavailable','Check ASTRA_DB points to your new writable temp directory. Do not rename/delete a locked existing database or select a sealed fixture.'],['No data / UNKNOWN','Check crew, source times, source quality and monitoring readiness. A paused or missing source can correctly be UNKNOWN.'],['Scenario unresponsive','Wait for pending operation; inspect current run, clock and role. Do not repeatedly issue a new Start.'],['Waveform missing / invisible','Check crew, recording, provided channel, cursor, cutoff and missing intervals. Import only an eligible synthetic example.'],['3D fails / WebGL unavailable','Use textual region controls. Check local assets, browser graphics support and explicit reload after context loss. Coarse LOD can reduce cost.'],['3D slow / navigation seems delayed','Allow the measured initial 8–9 s remount. Avoid duplicate tabs. Use coarse quality and reduced motion where appropriate.'],['AI unavailable','Expected for restricted Qwen, unreviewed support rules and operational N16. Use permitted lexical lookup or recorded evidence instead.'],['Logout hidden / session expired','Use the current responsive menu/Logout control; zoom/reflow is supported. 401: login again. 403: use a permitted role, not a bypass.']],[33,67])+refs('services/api/server.mjs','services/api/auth.mjs','docs/ASTRA_FINAL_DEMO_READINESS.md'),'compact')
u('One-page quick reference',h('Launch a fresh isolated WSL demo')+code('cd /mnt/c/users/basim/onedrive/desktop/astra-space-medical-ai\ndemo_dir=$(mktemp -d /tmp/astra-presentation-XXXXXXXX)\nexport ASTRA_DB="$demo_dir/astra.sqlite"\nexport HOST=127.0.0.1 PORT=3000 ASTRA_SPEED=1\nnpm start')+p('<strong>Open:</strong> http://127.0.0.1:3000 · <strong>Role:</strong> Demo administrator.<br><strong>Stop:</strong> Ctrl+C. <strong>Recover:</strong> keep the same ASTRA_DB and rerun npm start. A new temp directory creates a different demo, not recovery.')+h('Navigation you can rehearse')+flow('Figure U7. The recommended live demonstration remains within authorized synthetic interfaces.',['Overview → CREW-03 → Scenario lab / drift / advance 300 s','Crew health → N02 evidence → human acknowledgement','Anatomy / cardiovascular → Signal archive / replay','Switch crew → research evidence / exact lexical quotation'])+cols(h('What to show judges')+ul('Actual synthetic observations, units and time.','Deterministic alert persistence and human acknowledgement.','Crew-bound 3D selection, history and honest UNKNOWN.','Offline source attribution and recovery.'),h('What not to claim')+ul('Real astronaut sensors or clinical diagnosis.','AI emergency detection or a promoted Isolation Forest.','Validated forecasting, Qwen answering in the app or active N16 dispatch.','NASA endorsement, AC-20 PASS or flight certification.'))+h('Where to look when something fails')+p('The server terminal contains launch/runtime errors. The browser’s Developer Tools Console/Network can help explain a failed request; do not expose session tokens in a presentation. Existing acceptance reports and backups live in artifacts/. Runtime observations live at your chosen ASTRA_DB, not in those historical report folders.')+box('<strong>Next study resource:</strong> <a href="../../ASTRA - Technical Architecture and Project Report.pdf">ASTRA - Technical Architecture and Project Report.pdf</a>, in the project root. It explains the code, algorithms, database, scientific boundaries and 30 judges’ questions.')+refs('docs/ASTRA_FINAL_DEMO_READINESS.md','docs/demo/PRESENTATION_CHECKLIST.md','package.json','services/api/server.mjs'))
